# TypeScript security

## Secrets

```typescript
// NEVER
const apiKey = "sk-..."

// ALWAYS
const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_SOME_PUBLIC_KEY // only if truly public
```

- Service role keys and DB secrets: server-side / Supabase RLS only — never in client bundles
- Validate required env vars at startup on server paths

## Input validation

Validate all external input with Zod (or equivalent) at boundaries — forms, API handlers, RPC args.

## Supabase client

- Browser uses anon key + RLS
- Never bypass RLS from client code
- Parameterized queries via Supabase client — no string-concatenated SQL in app code

## Review trigger

Use `security-reviewer` agent when touching auth, roles, user input, or `supabase/migrations/`.
